    <string name="set_dual_vpn">Dual VPN</string>
    <string name="set_dual_enable">Enable Dual VPN</string>
    <string name="set_dual_desc">Sends your connections through two SOCKS5 servers, so neither server knows both who you are and where you go. SOCKS5 carries TCP only; see below for what that means.</string>
    <string name="set_hop1">First hop (server 1)</string>
    <string name="set_hop2">Second hop (server 2)</string>
    <string name="set_host">Host</string>
    <string name="set_port">Port</string>
    <string name="set_username_opt">Username (optional)</string>
    <string name="set_password_opt">Password (optional)</string>
    <string name="set_dual_flow">Through the chain (You → Hop 1 → Hop 2 → Internet): every TCP connection, and your DNS lookups when DoH (encrypted DNS) is on.\nNot through the chain: plain DNS when DoH is off goes straight to your resolver, so turn on DoH. QUIC (UDP port 443) is always blocked while Dual VPN is on, so apps fall back to TCP through the chain. Other UDP (calls, games, video chat) goes direct, unless you turn on the switch below.</string>
